WEBVTT

00:00:10.224 --> 00:00:40.536
The Bottle Imp by Robert Louis Stevenson Copyright Black Cat Publishing Robert Louis Stevenson was born in Edinburgh, Scotland in November 1850.

00:00:40.596 --> 00:00:47.650
When he was a child, his father told him stories of pirates and adventures.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:51.652
Robert liked these stories very much.

00:00:51.712 --> 00:01:01.779
When he went to university, he first studied engineering, but he did not like it, so he decided to study law.

00:01:01.839 --> 00:01:08.764
But he never worked as a lawyer because his dream was to become a writer.

00:01:08.824 --> 00:01:11.415
And his dream came true.

00:01:11.475 --> 00:01:19.280
He became a popular writer and wrote novels, short stories, and poems.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:22.702
He wrote a lot of stories.

00:01:22.762 --> 00:01:27.534
Many of them are adventures and fantasy stories.

00:01:27.594 --> 00:01:32.101
He is very popular as a writer of children's stories.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:42.990
because he wrote famous stories such as Treasure Island, 1883, and kidnapped 1886.

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:51.264
Another very famous children's classic is the Black Arrow, 1888.

00:01:51.324 --> 00:02:01.006
His great success was the strange case of Dr. Jekyll and Mr. Hyde, 1886.

00:02:01.066 --> 00:02:06.505
It is the story of a doctor and a drug he discovers.

00:02:06.565 --> 00:02:12.379
This changes him from a good person into a monster.

00:02:12.439 --> 00:02:18.034
Stevenson suffered from tuberculosis and was often ill.

00:02:18.094 --> 00:02:23.727
Scotland is a cold and wet country and this did not help him.

00:02:23.786 --> 00:02:31.735
So he decided to leave Scotland and travel to Spain and France because there was warm weather.

00:02:31.795 --> 00:02:36.330
His first books describe his time there.

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:45.004
During a trip in California in 1876, he met an American woman, Fanny Osborne.

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:51.618
He fell in love with her, but she was already married.

00:02:51.678 --> 00:02:59.939
In 1879, Fanny Osborne divorced her husband, and in 1880, she married Stevenson.

00:02:59.999 --> 00:03:07.518
In 1888, they decided to go to the South Seas.

00:03:07.578 --> 00:03:15.940
They visited many islands in the Pacific, including Tahiti, Samoa and Hawaii.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:22.681
They enjoyed this trip very much and decided to move to the island of Samoa.

00:03:22.741 --> 00:03:26.882
Stevenson continued to write many stories.

00:03:26.942 --> 00:03:35.905
In 1891, inspired by his visit to Hawaii, he wrote The Bottle Imp.

00:03:35.965 --> 00:03:44.702
In 1893, he published this story in a collection of eight stories called Island Nights Entertainment.

00:03:44.762 --> 00:03:49.996
All of these stories were about the islands in the Pacific.

00:03:50.056 --> 00:03:56.800
Robert Louis Stevenson died in Samoa on the 3rd of December, 1894.

00:03:56.860 --> 00:04:00.261
He was 44 years old.

00:04:00.321 --> 00:04:08.534
The islanders decided to bury him on Mount Vahia.

00:04:08.594 --> 00:04:14.347
Listening activity.

00:04:14.406 --> 00:04:16.948
A.

00:04:17.008 --> 00:04:21.770
As sailor works on a boat.

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:25.074
B.

00:04:25.134 --> 00:04:35.370
Passengers and objects can travel on a ship.

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:45.232
You can keep clothes and other objects in a chest.

00:04:45.292 --> 00:04:49.904
A pocket is sometimes part of your clothing.

00:04:49.964 --> 00:04:54.952
You can carry things here.

00:04:55.012 --> 00:05:03.852
A coin is a small round piece of metal used as money.

00:05:03.912 --> 00:05:12.655
F A bottle is a glass or plastic container.

00:05:12.714 --> 00:05:21.887
G A hill isn't a mountain, but it is very high.

00:05:21.907 --> 00:05:32.854
H A harbour is an area near the coast and you can leave your boat there.

00:05:32.914 --> 00:05:43.638
I, an imp, is a small creature with magical powers.

00:05:43.698 --> 00:05:57.145
CHAPTER I A STRANGE MEETING KI-A-WE was a courageous but poor man from Hawaii.

00:05:57.205 --> 00:06:01.938
His real name is secret because he is still alive.

00:06:01.998 --> 00:06:07.332
He could read and write and he was an excellent sailor.

00:06:07.391 --> 00:06:11.964
One day he decided to go and see the world.

00:06:12.024 --> 00:06:15.446
So he went on a ship to San Francisco.

00:06:15.506 --> 00:06:22.173
The city was beautiful with a lovely harbor and there were many rich people.

00:06:22.233 --> 00:06:26.760
One day, Kiare went for a walk on a hill.

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:29.432
There were some beautiful houses.

00:06:29.492 --> 00:06:31.694
He looked at them and thought.

00:06:31.754 --> 00:06:33.987
These houses are nice.

00:06:34.046 --> 00:06:37.080
The people must be very happy.

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:41.694
They are rich, so they don't worry about the future.

00:06:41.754 --> 00:06:45.738
He arrived at a small but lovely house.

00:06:45.797 --> 00:06:48.589
A man looked out of a window.

00:06:48.649 --> 00:06:53.722
Kiare looked at him and the man looked at Kiare too.

00:06:53.782 --> 00:06:55.884
The man was old.

00:06:55.944 --> 00:06:59.718
He was bald and had a long black beard.

00:06:59.778 --> 00:07:02.962
He seemed to be very unhappy.

00:07:03.022 --> 00:07:13.476
Kiare was envious of the man because he had a beautiful house, but the old man was also envious of Kiare.

00:07:13.536 --> 00:07:19.282
Suddenly the old man said, come and see my house.

00:07:19.342 --> 00:07:24.963
He showed Kiawe every room and Kiawe was very surprised.

00:07:25.023 --> 00:07:27.524
The house was perfect.

00:07:27.584 --> 00:07:31.125
You live in a beautiful house.

00:07:31.185 --> 00:07:33.295
Why are you so sad?

00:07:33.355 --> 00:07:35.036
Asked Kiawe.

00:07:35.096 --> 00:07:38.927
You can have a house like this.

00:07:38.987 --> 00:07:41.198
Do you have any money?

00:07:41.258 --> 00:07:43.092
Asked the old man.

00:07:43.152 --> 00:07:53.774
Ki-Aoue shook his head sadly and said, I only have $50, so I can't buy a beautiful house like this.

00:07:53.834 --> 00:08:00.020
I am sorry you do not have much money, so take this.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:03.272
It is yours for $50.

00:08:03.331 --> 00:08:04.843
The house?

00:08:04.903 --> 00:08:07.315
asked Ki-Aoue surprised.

00:08:07.375 --> 00:08:10.274
No, the bottle.

00:08:10.334 --> 00:08:18.736
Because all I have comes from this small bottle.

00:08:18.796 --> 00:08:28.262
Listening activity What is an imp?

00:08:28.322 --> 00:08:31.844
An imp is a type of genie.

00:08:31.904 --> 00:08:37.964
It is usually a sleep and prisoner inside a bottle or a lamp.

00:08:38.024 --> 00:08:49.426
When somebody wakes it up, the imp must serve this person with its magical powers, and sometimes make their wishes come true.

00:08:49.486 --> 00:08:53.599
An imp can be good or evil.

00:08:53.659 --> 00:08:59.272
Usually, bad imps play horrible jokes on people.

00:08:59.332 --> 00:09:05.678
You can read about a famous genie in A Thousand and One Nights.

00:09:05.738 --> 00:09:14.114
A boy, Aladdin, finds a magic oil lamp, but he does not know there is a genie inside.

00:09:14.174 --> 00:09:22.610
Suddenly, it comes out of the lamp and gives him three wishes.

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:35.987
Chapter 2 The Bottle Imp The old man showed Ki'awe a round bottle with a long neck.

00:09:36.047 --> 00:09:40.578
It was white, but there were also many different colors.

00:09:40.638 --> 00:09:43.450
The colors of the rainbow.

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:46.532
Kiare looked at it closely.

00:09:46.592 --> 00:09:52.026
He saw the colors change and he saw something inside move.

00:09:52.086 --> 00:09:59.790
The old man said, You can't break this bottle because it is magic.

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:05.481
It comes from hell and inside there is an imp.

00:10:05.541 --> 00:10:09.031
This imp is very powerful.

00:10:09.090 --> 00:10:12.372
You can have everything you want.

00:10:12.432 --> 00:10:20.780
Love, money, Napoleon and Captain Cook bought it, and they became powerful.

00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:23.582
So why do you want to sell it?

00:10:23.642 --> 00:10:25.413
Asked Kiare.

00:10:25.473 --> 00:10:29.806
The imp cannot make me live for a long time.

00:10:29.866 --> 00:10:34.616
I am old, and I must sell it before I die.

00:10:34.676 --> 00:10:38.396
because I don't want to burn in hell forever.

00:10:38.456 --> 00:10:43.689
Well, I don't want to burn in hell, so I won't buy it.

00:10:43.749 --> 00:10:45.240
Said Kiyawe.

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:49.722
You can buy the bottle and then sell it one day.

00:10:49.782 --> 00:10:51.824
You can be very happy.

00:10:51.884 --> 00:10:53.726
Said the old man.

00:10:53.786 --> 00:10:56.808
Kiyawe was confused.

00:10:56.868 --> 00:11:00.780
There are two things that I can't understand.

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:06.094
The bottle can make you happy, but you are very sad.

00:11:06.154 --> 00:11:11.738
And the bottle can make you powerful, but it is very cheap.

00:11:11.798 --> 00:11:21.914
The old man said, I am sad because I am old and ill, and I must sell this bottle before I die.

00:11:21.974 --> 00:11:31.276
In the past, the bottle was very expensive, but every time someone sells it, the price must go down.

00:11:31.336 --> 00:11:36.914
You cannot sell the bottle for more money or for the same amount of money.

00:11:36.974 --> 00:11:39.575
It always returns to you.

00:11:39.635 --> 00:11:43.356
Also, you must pay with coins.

00:11:43.416 --> 00:11:47.048
People do not believe you because it is so cheap.

00:11:47.108 --> 00:11:49.308
Why don't you try it?

00:11:49.368 --> 00:11:52.490
Give me your $50 and make a wish.

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:55.361
Wish for another $50.

00:11:55.421 --> 00:12:01.006
So Kyawe gave the old man the money and wished for $50.

00:12:01.066 --> 00:12:06.082
Immediately there was another $50 in his pocket.

00:12:06.142 --> 00:12:13.448
Kiowa was very surprised, but he was also afraid and didn't want to keep the bottle.

00:12:13.508 --> 00:12:17.802
The old man said, It is yours now.

00:12:17.862 --> 00:12:22.375
Goodbye.

00:12:22.435 --> 00:12:27.630
Captain Cook.

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:30.435
Captain James Cook.

00:12:30.495 --> 00:12:36.581
was a very famous British explorer, navigator and cartographer.

00:12:36.641 --> 00:12:41.103
He was also an astronomer and a mathematician.

00:12:41.164 --> 00:12:48.418
He was born in 1728 in Yorkshire, in the north east of England.

00:12:48.478 --> 00:12:53.570
He went to the local school and then he worked on a farm.

00:12:53.630 --> 00:13:04.884
In 1755 a war started between England and France This war didn't finish until 1763.

00:13:04.944 --> 00:13:14.266
Cook decided to enter the Royal Navy and took part in several expeditions in Canada and the Pacific Ocean.

00:13:14.326 --> 00:13:18.318
He became an expert cartographer.

00:13:18.377 --> 00:13:25.059
After the war, the British government asked Cook to explore the Pacific.

00:13:25.119 --> 00:13:28.356
This was Cook's first voyage.

00:13:28.416 --> 00:13:35.238
In 1768, he left Plymouth in a single ship, the Endeavour.

00:13:35.298 --> 00:13:43.914
Between 1768 and 1771, he explored Tahiti and New Zealand.

00:13:43.974 --> 00:13:56.994
At that time, people believed there was a southern continent in the Pacific Ocean, and during his voyages, Captain Cook's secret mission was to find it.

00:13:57.054 --> 00:14:03.660
In 1770 he was successful and found Australia.

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:07.704
He explored and chartered its east coast.

00:14:07.764 --> 00:14:13.108
He claimed this area of land for King George III of England.

00:14:13.168 --> 00:14:18.924
He also gave it a name, New South Wales.

00:14:18.984 --> 00:14:25.338
Captain Cook was an intelligent man with a strong personality.

00:14:25.398 --> 00:14:30.470
At that time Many sailors died during the voyages.

00:14:30.530 --> 00:14:38.414
He introduced some rules of personal hygiene, and he and his men ate many vegetables and fruit.

00:14:38.474 --> 00:14:42.896
As a result, less sailors died.

00:14:42.956 --> 00:14:56.195
On his second voyage, between 1772 and 1775, he was the first person to go around Antarctica and the globe from west to east.

00:14:56.254 --> 00:15:01.550
This was a very difficult voyage because of the cold weather.

00:15:01.610 --> 00:15:10.856
Cook and his men spent the winter months in New Zealand and Tahiti and the summer months exploring the Antarctic.

00:15:10.916 --> 00:15:20.280
He discovered many islands, including a group of 15 islands in the South Pacific between Hawaii and New Zealand.

00:15:20.340 --> 00:15:25.420
He called these islands the Cook Islands.

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:35.802
On his third expedition to the Pacific Ocean in 1778, he discovered and explored the Hawaiian Islands.

00:15:35.862 --> 00:15:39.524
He called them the Sandwich Islands.

00:15:39.584 --> 00:15:43.666
His patron was the Earl of Sandwich.

00:15:43.726 --> 00:15:53.623
He also tried to find a new route to the East Indies, a northwest passage around Canada and Alaska.

00:15:53.683 --> 00:15:57.526
but this time he was not successful.

00:15:57.586 --> 00:16:10.064
During this voyage he found a lot of ice and so he decided to return to Hawaii for the winter and find food and drink for his next voyage.

00:16:10.124 --> 00:16:25.774
At first he had a good relationship with the natives of Hawaii and they were friendly but then things changed and they killed him in 1779.

00:16:25.834 --> 00:16:42.774
Chapter 3 Ki-Awe's Wish Comes True At first Ki-Awe thought the bottle wasn't really magical, so he left it in the middle of the road.

00:16:42.834 --> 00:16:48.788
But when he turned the corner, the bottle was once again in his pocket.

00:16:48.848 --> 00:16:53.590
Then he bought a corkscrew and tried to open the bottle.

00:16:53.651 --> 00:16:55.892
But it was impossible.

00:16:55.952 --> 00:16:59.593
He suddenly became very afraid.

00:16:59.653 --> 00:17:04.284
He went into a shop and sold it for $60.

00:17:04.344 --> 00:17:08.806
But later he found the bottle in his chest.

00:17:08.867 --> 00:17:15.880
Kiawe told his good friend Lopaka the story and asked him to keep it a secret.

00:17:15.940 --> 00:17:22.754
Lopaka told him, I am afraid this bottle will give you problems.

00:17:22.814 --> 00:17:29.680
Decide what you want from it and then sell it to me because I have a project.

00:17:29.740 --> 00:17:37.556
I want a sailing ship, so that I can travel and buy and sell many objects on the islands.

00:17:37.616 --> 00:17:46.170
Kiawe thought for a moment and then said, My dream is to have a beautiful house in Hawaii.

00:17:46.231 --> 00:17:50.673
I want to be happy there with my family and friends.

00:17:50.733 --> 00:17:55.540
So Kiawe and Lopaka decided to go to Hawaii.

00:17:55.600 --> 00:18:01.478
When they arrived, an old friend met them and said to Kiawe.

00:18:01.538 --> 00:18:07.479
I'm very sorry, but your uncle and cousin died while you were away.

00:18:07.539 --> 00:18:10.860
Kiawe was very sad.

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:13.710
Lupaka told his friend.

00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:20.882
Your uncle's land is yours now, and you can build the house of your dreams.

00:18:20.942 --> 00:18:24.511
But Kiawe was very unhappy.

00:18:24.571 --> 00:18:28.220
Did the imp kill his relatives?

00:18:28.280 --> 00:18:32.574
Kiare and Lepaka went to see a lawyer.

00:18:32.634 --> 00:18:39.028
Kiare discovered that his uncle was very rich and he now had a lot of money.

00:18:39.088 --> 00:18:45.721
The lawyer told them about a brilliant new architect, so they went to see him.

00:18:45.782 --> 00:18:52.106
When they arrived, the architect already had a drawing of a house on his table.

00:18:52.166 --> 00:18:54.617
Kiare was surprised.

00:18:54.677 --> 00:18:56.618
It was perfect.

00:18:56.678 --> 00:18:59.579
It was the house of his dreams.

00:18:59.639 --> 00:19:06.432
The architect wanted exactly the same amount of money that Kiare received from his uncle.

00:19:06.492 --> 00:19:13.196
Kiare said it was his destiny to have this house and signed a contract.

00:19:13.256 --> 00:19:17.198
But he also thought about the old man's words.

00:19:17.258 --> 00:19:20.524
It comes from hell.

00:19:20.585 --> 00:19:28.102
Kiare decided not to make any more wishes and he and Lepaka left for Australia.

00:19:28.162 --> 00:19:34.744
They wanted to return when the house was ready.

00:19:34.804 --> 00:19:43.238
Chapter 4 Kiare sells the bottle.

00:19:43.298 --> 00:19:51.426
When they returned to Hawaii, the house was ready and it was exactly what Kiare wanted.

00:19:51.486 --> 00:19:58.636
The rooms, the furniture, the ornaments, the garden, everything was beautiful.

00:19:58.696 --> 00:20:05.519
Lopaka said, it is possible that the imp has nothing to do with this.

00:20:05.580 --> 00:20:13.504
I promise to buy the bottle from you, but before I do, I want to be sure that it really has power.

00:20:13.564 --> 00:20:18.668
Kiawa replied, I can't ask the imp for another wish.

00:20:18.728 --> 00:20:20.402
I promised.

00:20:20.462 --> 00:20:23.072
I only want to see the Imp.

00:20:23.132 --> 00:20:24.293
Said Lepaka.

00:20:24.353 --> 00:20:27.584
Then I will buy the bottle from you.

00:20:27.644 --> 00:20:32.586
Kiare was afraid, but he was all so curious.

00:20:32.646 --> 00:20:36.117
So he ordered the Imp to come out of the bottle.

00:20:36.177 --> 00:20:38.328
Come out now!

00:20:38.388 --> 00:20:44.972
The Imp looked out, but disappeared inside again immediately.

00:20:45.032 --> 00:20:49.837
Kiaway and Lopaka were very shocked and terrified.

00:20:49.897 --> 00:20:53.178
They could not move or speak for hours.

00:20:53.238 --> 00:20:58.342
Finally Lopaka said, I want to keep my promise.

00:20:58.402 --> 00:21:00.542
So here is the money.

00:21:00.602 --> 00:21:06.435
I will buy my ship and then I will sell this bottle as soon as possible.

00:21:06.495 --> 00:21:16.552
Kiaway said, It is night and the roads are bad, but I can't sleep, eat or pray with this bottle in my house.

00:21:16.612 --> 00:21:21.757
So please take what you want from my house and leave now."

00:21:21.817 --> 00:21:27.032
Lopaka was afraid too, but he understood his friend.

00:21:27.092 --> 00:21:30.706
He wished Ki-Awe good luck and left.

00:21:30.766 --> 00:21:40.069
As Ki-Awe watched his friend leave, He prayed for him, but he was also very happy that he didn't have the bottle.

00:21:40.129 --> 00:21:46.104
Kiawa loved his house and many people came to visit and admire it.

00:21:46.164 --> 00:21:50.158
One day he saw a beautiful girl swimming in the sea.

00:21:50.218 --> 00:21:52.950
He immediately fell in love with her.

00:21:53.010 --> 00:21:55.162
Her name was Kakua.

00:21:55.222 --> 00:22:00.526
He did not tell her his name because he did not want her to know he was rich.

00:22:00.586 --> 00:22:03.338
She took him to her father's house.

00:22:03.398 --> 00:22:14.657
Keanu, her father, knew Keawe, and the girl understood that he was very rich and that he wanted to marry her.

00:22:14.717 --> 00:22:20.312
Listening activity.

00:22:20.372 --> 00:22:22.584
Hello, Kakua.

00:22:22.644 --> 00:22:23.904
It's Keawe.

00:22:23.964 --> 00:22:25.406
Hello, Keawe.

00:22:25.466 --> 00:22:26.536
How are you?

00:22:26.596 --> 00:22:27.948
Fine, thanks.

00:22:28.008 --> 00:22:31.750
I'm calling because I want to invite you to a concert.

00:22:31.810 --> 00:22:35.521
I have two tickets for the Hawaii Flower Band concert.

00:22:35.581 --> 00:22:36.612
Great.

00:22:36.672 --> 00:22:38.372
I love their music.

00:22:38.432 --> 00:22:39.622
When is it?

00:22:39.682 --> 00:22:43.174
On Saturday afternoon at 6.15.

00:22:43.234 --> 00:22:44.234
Fine.

00:22:44.294 --> 00:22:45.855
When can we meet?

00:22:45.915 --> 00:22:48.456
We can meet at 5.30.

00:22:48.516 --> 00:22:49.846
Is that okay?

00:22:49.906 --> 00:22:50.876
Of course.

00:22:50.936 --> 00:22:52.537
Where is the concert?

00:22:52.597 --> 00:22:55.348
It's at the Hawaiian Arena.

00:22:55.408 --> 00:22:57.819
We can meet at the entrance.

00:22:57.879 --> 00:22:59.559
Do you know the address?

00:22:59.620 --> 00:23:01.571
No, I don't.

00:23:01.631 --> 00:23:04.773
It's 14, Gogan Road.

00:23:04.833 --> 00:23:06.714
How do you spell that?

00:23:06.774 --> 00:23:17.068
G, A, U, G, U, I, N.

00:23:17.128 --> 00:23:19.229
What can I wear?

00:23:19.289 --> 00:23:21.930
Casual clothes are okay.

00:23:21.990 --> 00:23:24.412
Just put on a pair of jeans.

00:23:24.471 --> 00:23:26.152
They are comfortable.

00:23:26.212 --> 00:23:27.272
Great.

00:23:27.332 --> 00:23:28.773
See you there then.

00:23:28.833 --> 00:23:29.923
Bye.

00:23:29.984 --> 00:23:35.341
Bye.

00:23:35.401 --> 00:23:48.680
The Hawaiian Islands are in the Pacific Ocean, about 2,500 miles west of San Francisco.

00:23:48.740 --> 00:23:56.092
They became part of the United States on the 21st of August, 1959.

00:23:56.153 --> 00:24:05.529
They are the 50th state of the United States and consist of 8 big islands and over 100 small ones.

00:24:05.589 --> 00:24:10.756
Most of the population live on six islands.

00:24:10.816 --> 00:24:21.413
Hawaii, Kauai, Lanai, Maui, Molokai and Oahu.

00:24:21.473 --> 00:24:25.015
Some history.

00:24:25.075 --> 00:24:33.066
From the 16th century, people from Tahiti and the Marquesas Islands occupied this land.

00:24:33.126 --> 00:24:40.136
The first European to discover these islands was kept in Cook in 1778.

00:24:40.196 --> 00:24:50.542
At the beginning of the 19th century missionaries, tradesmen and whale hunters arrived from England and the USA.

00:24:50.602 --> 00:25:01.036
Unfortunately they also brought many new diseases and consequently 80% of the native population died.

00:25:01.096 --> 00:25:10.798
These islands became very important for their production of sugar cane and many immigrants arrived.

00:25:10.858 --> 00:25:23.792
In 1941, the Japanese attacked the famous Pearl Harbor US military base on the Oahu Island and the USA entered the Second World War as a result.

00:25:23.852 --> 00:25:36.442
Hawaii Today Today, the main economic activities of these islands are tourism and the growing of sugar cane and pineapples.

00:25:36.502 --> 00:25:42.036
The capital of the state is Honolulu on the Oahu Island.

00:25:42.096 --> 00:25:45.758
This island has the most tourists.

00:25:45.818 --> 00:25:57.312
On their arrival, the tourists can relax on the many wonderful beaches of white sand and swim in the incredibly blue water of the ocean.

00:25:57.372 --> 00:26:11.354
Some important symbols of Hawaii are hula dances, the lay flowers, grass skirts, ukulele, Hawaiian music.

00:26:11.414 --> 00:26:15.585
For surfers, the best island is Maui.

00:26:15.645 --> 00:26:19.576
Here, there are also spectacular beaches.

00:26:19.636 --> 00:26:24.257
The island of Kauai is called the Garden Island.

00:26:24.317 --> 00:26:28.342
It has many beautiful rivers and waterfalls.

00:26:28.402 --> 00:26:33.117
Big Island is the second name of the island of Hawaii.

00:26:33.177 --> 00:26:39.450
Its capital is called Hilo and the island is famous for its volcanoes.

00:26:39.510 --> 00:26:45.514
Particularly famous are Mauna Kea and Kilauea crater.

00:26:45.574 --> 00:26:52.357
Mauna Kea is 4,025 meters high and is a sleeping volcano.

00:26:52.417 --> 00:26:56.708
Sometimes you even see some snow at the top.

00:26:56.768 --> 00:27:02.940
Kiawea crater is a very active volcano and erupts regularly.

00:27:03.000 --> 00:27:10.192
Luckily, these eruptions are usually very small.

00:27:10.252 --> 00:27:18.866
Chapter 5 Kiawe must find the bottle again.

00:27:18.926 --> 00:27:24.793
Kiawea was very happy and he sang when he went home.

00:27:24.853 --> 00:27:33.404
He sang when he ate his dinner on the balcony, and his Chinese servant heard him sing when he prepared his bath.

00:27:33.464 --> 00:27:37.388
Suddenly, the singing stopped.

00:27:37.448 --> 00:27:43.294
When Ki-Awe took off his clothes, he saw a mark on his body.

00:27:43.354 --> 00:27:46.026
He understood immediately.

00:27:46.086 --> 00:27:48.570
He had leprosy.

00:27:48.630 --> 00:27:59.142
In a moment, all his dreams disappeared, and he was desperate because he knew it was impossible to marry Kakua.

00:27:59.202 --> 00:28:03.306
Then he suddenly thought of the bottle.

00:28:03.366 --> 00:28:06.638
The bottle could cure his illness.

00:28:06.698 --> 00:28:09.922
It was his only possibility.

00:28:09.982 --> 00:28:13.774
He wanted to marry Kakua very much.

00:28:13.834 --> 00:28:19.112
He was afraid, but he decided to look for Lopaka.

00:28:19.173 --> 00:28:25.149
Somebody told him Lopaka had a big ship, but he was far away.

00:28:25.209 --> 00:28:29.850
He thought of Lopaka's friends and remembered the lawyer.

00:28:29.911 --> 00:28:35.672
He discovered that he was very rich now and had a lovely house on a beach.

00:28:35.732 --> 00:28:44.075
When he saw Kiawe, the lawyer seemed worried, but he gave Kiawe the name of another person.

00:28:44.135 --> 00:28:50.158
Kiawe met a lot of rich people, but nobody had the bottle.

00:28:50.218 --> 00:28:54.781
Finally, one evening he found a young man.

00:28:54.842 --> 00:28:57.844
This man was rich like the others.

00:28:57.904 --> 00:29:00.305
But he looked terrible.

00:29:00.365 --> 00:29:06.098
His face was white, and he had dark rings around his eyes.

00:29:06.158 --> 00:29:10.292
Kiawe knew that this was the person.

00:29:10.352 --> 00:29:13.054
He had the bottle.

00:29:13.114 --> 00:29:17.183
Kiawe said, I am here to buy the bottle.

00:29:17.242 --> 00:29:18.730
The barking?

00:29:18.790 --> 00:29:20.480
To buy the barking?

00:29:20.540 --> 00:29:21.830
He whispered.

00:29:21.890 --> 00:29:22.911
Yes.

00:29:22.971 --> 00:29:24.832
How much does it cost now?

00:29:24.892 --> 00:29:26.702
Asked Kiawe.

00:29:26.762 --> 00:29:32.084
The man was shocked and the glass in his hand fell to the floor.

00:29:32.144 --> 00:29:34.726
The price?

00:29:34.786 --> 00:29:37.676
Don't you know the price?

00:29:37.736 --> 00:29:41.478
I paid two cents for it.

00:29:41.538 --> 00:29:42.822
He said.

00:29:42.882 --> 00:29:44.806
Kiare answered.

00:29:44.866 --> 00:29:51.962
So you can only sell it for one cent and the person who buys it.

00:29:52.022 --> 00:29:54.734
He could not finish the sentence.

00:29:54.794 --> 00:29:56.694
He understood.

00:29:56.754 --> 00:30:00.268
He could never sell the bottle again.

00:30:00.328 --> 00:30:05.112
The young man fell on his knees and begged him.

00:30:05.172 --> 00:30:07.553
Please buy the bottle.

00:30:07.613 --> 00:30:13.505
I will give you everything I have.

00:30:13.565 --> 00:30:21.066
Chapter 6 A great idea.

00:30:21.126 --> 00:30:25.238
Ki-Awe gave the man one cent.

00:30:25.298 --> 00:30:29.209
He made his wish and then he took the bottle.

00:30:29.269 --> 00:30:31.600
He looked in a mirror.

00:30:31.660 --> 00:30:33.710
It was a miracle.

00:30:33.770 --> 00:30:36.562
The mark was not there.

00:30:36.622 --> 00:30:42.514
The problem now was that he did not care about his health or for kakua.

00:30:42.574 --> 00:30:47.006
He thought only about the bottle imp and his destiny.

00:30:47.066 --> 00:30:49.838
He was very depressed.

00:30:49.898 --> 00:30:54.770
Ki-Awe remembered that there was a concert in town that evening.

00:30:54.830 --> 00:30:59.281
He decided to go because he did not want to be alone.

00:30:59.341 --> 00:31:07.744
Courage returned to him when they played Kakua's and his song, and he decided to return to Hawaii.

00:31:07.804 --> 00:31:12.736
He married Kakua and carried her to his beautiful house.

00:31:12.796 --> 00:31:17.287
When they were together, he was very happy and calm.

00:31:17.347 --> 00:31:23.418
but when he was alone, he was always very worried and depressed.

00:31:23.478 --> 00:31:35.431
Kokua loved him very much and brought him much happiness, but Kokua saw that Kiawe was unhappy, and she didn't understand.

00:31:35.491 --> 00:31:40.852
She thought that she was responsible and decided to ask him.

00:31:40.912 --> 00:31:46.614
She told him, Before we married, you were always happy.

00:31:46.674 --> 00:31:50.328
But now you do not smile anymore."

00:31:50.388 --> 00:31:57.193
Ki-Awe told her his story so she could understand how much he loved her.

00:31:57.254 --> 00:32:02.448
Kukua cried and said, I will save you.

00:32:02.508 --> 00:32:05.801
You cannot help me.

00:32:05.861 --> 00:32:08.673
He answered sadly.

00:32:08.734 --> 00:32:14.089
But Kukua said, I went to school in Honolulu.

00:32:14.149 --> 00:32:15.830
I'm not stupid.

00:32:15.890 --> 00:32:22.712
There are other countries in the world where people use different money, like in England and France.

00:32:22.772 --> 00:32:27.684
For one cent, we can have four French Saint-Teams.

00:32:27.744 --> 00:32:31.696
Let's go to the French islands, to Tahiti.

00:32:31.756 --> 00:32:37.818
We can sell the bottle for some teams.

00:32:37.878 --> 00:32:46.562
Chapter 7 Ki-Awe can't sell the bottle.

00:32:46.622 --> 00:32:52.335
Ki-Awe was very happy and they prepared for the voyage.

00:32:52.395 --> 00:32:58.638
They took all their best clothes and jewels because they wanted to seem rich.

00:32:58.698 --> 00:33:02.580
This was important to sell the bottle imp.

00:33:02.640 --> 00:33:09.669
When they arrived, they rented an ice house, a carriage and some horses.

00:33:09.729 --> 00:33:15.219
Cokua was very courageous and used the bottle imp for money.

00:33:15.279 --> 00:33:22.404
They learned the local language and when they could speak it, they tried to sell the bottle.

00:33:22.464 --> 00:33:25.097
It was very difficult.

00:33:25.157 --> 00:33:30.412
People didn't think they were honest because the bottle was so cheap.

00:33:30.471 --> 00:33:36.536
People avoided them and Kiawe and Cokua were very depressed.

00:33:36.596 --> 00:33:41.303
They could not sleep at night because they were afraid.

00:33:41.363 --> 00:33:46.768
One night, Kukua woke up, but her husband was not in bed.

00:33:46.827 --> 00:33:52.382
She found him under the banana trees, crying silently.

00:33:52.442 --> 00:33:56.346
She understood that she must save him.

00:33:56.406 --> 00:34:00.260
She left the house and went for a walk.

00:34:00.320 --> 00:34:07.367
She saw a poor old man under a tree, a stranger on the island.

00:34:07.427 --> 00:34:10.830
And she told him their story.

00:34:10.890 --> 00:34:16.072
She asked him to go to Kiawe and buy the bottle.

00:34:16.132 --> 00:34:22.684
Then she wanted to buy the bottle from the old man and save her husband.

00:34:22.745 --> 00:34:29.107
So the old man went to Kiawe, bought the bottle and came back.

00:34:29.167 --> 00:34:33.128
Your husband cried with happiness.

00:34:33.189 --> 00:34:35.800
I am sure he was sleep tonight.

00:34:35.860 --> 00:34:37.261
He said.

00:34:37.321 --> 00:34:48.096
At first, Kukua hesitated, but then courage came back to her and she bought the bottle back from him and went home.

00:34:48.156 --> 00:34:56.088
Her husband slept like a child, but she couldn't sleep or be happy.

00:34:56.149 --> 00:35:00.540
When Ki-Awe woke up, he was very pleased.

00:35:00.600 --> 00:35:05.212
He did not notice that Kukua was sad and could not eat.

00:35:05.272 --> 00:35:07.565
He told her the story.

00:35:07.626 --> 00:35:14.122
thanked her, planned their return home and laughed at the stupid old man.

00:35:14.182 --> 00:35:21.466
Kiawe was angry because Kokua was not happy and he left her alone.

00:35:21.526 --> 00:35:29.422
When he came back, he told her she was not a good wife because she was not happy for him.

00:35:29.482 --> 00:35:35.972
Kiawe left the house and went out with some friends and they drank a lot.

00:35:36.032 --> 00:35:43.863
One of the drinkers, a sailor and an ex-prisoner, was a bad and dishonest person.

00:35:43.923 --> 00:35:52.218
He wanted an expensive drink, and so he said, Hey, Ki-Awe, you are very rich.

00:35:52.278 --> 00:35:55.941
Bring some money so we can buy some rum.

00:35:56.001 --> 00:36:01.475
Ki-Awe replied, I'll go home because my wife keeps our money.

00:36:01.535 --> 00:36:06.145
The sailor replied, Don't leave your money with her.

00:36:06.205 --> 00:36:08.923
You can never trust women.

00:36:08.983 --> 00:36:11.234
They are all false."

00:36:11.294 --> 00:36:20.137
Ki-Awe started to think this was true because Kokura was so unhappy.

00:36:20.197 --> 00:36:28.220
Chapter 8 A surprising end.

00:36:28.280 --> 00:36:35.878
When Ki-Awe went home and opened the door, he saw his wife with the bottle near her.

00:36:35.938 --> 00:36:39.658
he was very shocked and did not believe it.

00:36:39.718 --> 00:36:47.322
He immediately thought that the bottle was there again because there was an error when he sold it to the old man.

00:36:47.382 --> 00:36:51.446
He closed the door and waited for a moment.

00:36:51.506 --> 00:36:58.690
Then he opened it again, loudly, but this time the bottle was not there.

00:36:58.750 --> 00:37:06.768
He said to Kakua, I only want some money because I want to drink some expensive rum with my friends.

00:37:06.828 --> 00:37:13.500
He went to his chest and pretended to look for the money, but the bottle wasn't there.

00:37:13.560 --> 00:37:16.921
Finally, he understood.

00:37:16.981 --> 00:37:20.312
He stopped and looked at his wife.

00:37:20.372 --> 00:37:23.542
He knew that expression on her face.

00:37:23.602 --> 00:37:28.344
He was desperate, so he took some money and left the house.

00:37:28.404 --> 00:37:31.500
He did not want to drink now.

00:37:31.560 --> 00:37:36.896
He went to the bad sailor and said, My wife has the bottle.

00:37:36.956 --> 00:37:42.467
We can have money for a drink, but first you must help me.

00:37:42.527 --> 00:37:46.578
I must become the owner of that bottle again.

00:37:46.638 --> 00:37:49.048
Here are two saunteams.

00:37:49.108 --> 00:37:51.509
Go and buy the bottle from her.

00:37:51.569 --> 00:37:57.320
Then I will buy it from you, but don't tell her I am sending you.

00:37:57.380 --> 00:38:07.750
Then Ki always said, When you come out of the house with the bottle, you can make a wish for some money in your pocket or a very good bottle of rum.

00:38:07.810 --> 00:38:12.346
You will then understand that this bottle is magic.

00:38:12.406 --> 00:38:16.760
So the man left and Ki-Awe waited for him.

00:38:16.820 --> 00:38:19.252
His heart was bitter.

00:38:19.312 --> 00:38:22.168
He waited for a very long time.

00:38:22.228 --> 00:38:26.475
And then finally he heard the man's voice in the dark.

00:38:26.535 --> 00:38:28.586
He was very drunk.

00:38:28.647 --> 00:38:34.670
He had the devil's bottle in his pocket, and another bottle in his hand.

00:38:34.730 --> 00:38:36.452
Give me the bottle, Nell!

00:38:36.512 --> 00:38:37.762
Said Ki-Awe.

00:38:37.822 --> 00:38:39.164
Hands off!

00:38:39.224 --> 00:38:40.624
Cried the sailor.

00:38:40.685 --> 00:38:43.976
This is a good bottle.

00:38:44.036 --> 00:38:48.939
I can't understand how I got it for only two Santines.

00:38:48.999 --> 00:38:53.350
I certainly will not give it to you for once on, team.

00:38:53.410 --> 00:38:56.832
But I can give you some rump.

00:38:56.892 --> 00:38:59.904
Do you mean you will not sell it?

00:38:59.964 --> 00:39:01.865
But you will go to hell.

00:39:01.925 --> 00:39:03.295
Said Kiawe.

00:39:03.356 --> 00:39:05.747
I am already going to hell.

00:39:05.807 --> 00:39:07.848
And I like this bottle.

00:39:07.908 --> 00:39:09.869
Go and look for another one.

00:39:09.929 --> 00:39:11.890
The bad sailor answered.

00:39:11.950 --> 00:39:14.812
Please sell this bottle to me.

00:39:14.872 --> 00:39:16.708
Insisted Kiawe.

00:39:16.768 --> 00:39:20.765
I don't believe what you say about this bottle.

00:39:20.825 --> 00:39:26.087
You thought I was stupid, but now you can see I'm not.

00:39:26.147 --> 00:39:30.449
If you don't want any of this rum, I'll drink it.

00:39:30.509 --> 00:39:31.940
Good night."

00:39:32.000 --> 00:39:37.602
The sailor left, and the bottle disappeared from this story with him.

00:39:37.662 --> 00:39:41.154
Kiare ran to Kokua very fast.

00:39:41.214 --> 00:39:43.553
Their joy was great that night.

00:39:43.613 --> 00:39:52.658
And from that moment, they lived happily and peacefully in their lovely house.

00:39:52.718 --> 00:39:59.354
Listening activity.

00:39:59.414 --> 00:40:02.426
Hi, Susan.

00:40:02.486 --> 00:40:03.898
This is Emma.

00:40:03.958 --> 00:40:07.670
Do you have any ideas for Julia's birthday present?

00:40:07.730 --> 00:40:09.713
What about a book?

00:40:09.773 --> 00:40:12.696
Last week I read a really good story.

00:40:12.756 --> 00:40:14.717
It was called the bottle imp.

00:40:14.778 --> 00:40:17.570
The author is Robert Louis Stevenson.

00:40:17.630 --> 00:40:20.092
I know Julia will like it too.

00:40:20.152 --> 00:40:22.183
It's not very expensive.

00:40:22.243 --> 00:40:24.976
I bought it for three pans forty.

00:40:25.036 --> 00:40:28.398
Please meet me outside the book shop at four p.m.

00:40:28.438 --> 00:40:29.288
tomorrow.

00:40:29.348 --> 00:40:32.431
You can send me a text message to confirm.

00:40:32.491 --> 00:40:33.402
See you then.

